  "notes": {
    "residual_definition": "collocation_energy_balance_residual is measured on 2,000 collocation points sampled uniformly across the entire 5D input domain (including unvisited states), decoupled from test MAE.",
    "findings_summary": "1. Analytical Baseline: The analytical ODE formulas achieve an in-distribution SOC MAE of ~0.0002% and serve as the deterministic safety guardrail in the digital twin.\n2. In-Distribution Fitting: The unconstrained Plain MLP fits smooth training data closer than the PINN at dense data regimes (5%, 10%, 100%), achieving lower test SOC MAE. The PINN physics penalty acts as a regularizer that restricts unconstrained data memorization.\n3. Data-Scarcity Multi-Seed Reality: Across 5 random seeds, the 1% data regime exhibits high variance; neither model consistently dominates without adequate sample coverage.\n4. Collocation Invariants: The PINN consistently reduces energy balance and thermal dynamics violations on unvisited collocation points across the 5D state space, although soft penalties do not guarantee zero boundary violations on extreme collocation coordinates.\n5. Thermal Dynamics: Incorporating temp_prev resolves prior thermal tracking errors, bringing temperature MAE below 0.08\u00b0C for both architectures."
  }
